@startuml
title Course registration - domain class diagram
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

class Student {
  - studentId: String
  - fullName: String
}

class Course {
  - courseCode: String
  - title: String
}

class CourseOffering {
  - offeringId: String
  - semester: String
  - capacity: int
  + enrolledCount(): int
  + availablePlaces(): int
  + hasFreePlace(): boolean
}

class Enrollment {
  - enrollmentId: String
  - createdAt: DateTime
}

Course "1" -- "0..*" CourseOffering : offers >
Student "1" -- "0..*" Enrollment : holds >
CourseOffering "1" -- "0..*" Enrollment : records >

note bottom of CourseOffering
  Capacity constraint (R2):
  enrolledCount() <= capacity at all times.
  availablePlaces() = capacity - enrolledCount(),
  derived, not stored, because cancellation
  is out of scope.
end note

note bottom of Enrollment
  Uniqueness constraint (R3):
  the pair (Student, CourseOffering) is unique;
  a student holds at most one Enrollment
  in the same offering.
  Creation of an Enrollment together with the
  duplicate and capacity checks is one atomic
  operation (R4). Rejected requests create
  nothing (R5).
end note
@enduml
